  "content": "We still don't know how they managed to do all that. The recorded part of the story began later, Oct. 10, 2025. Marc Elias, threat intelligence analyst for the Symantec and Carbon Black Threat Hunter Team, recalls, \"The first signs of activity we observed on the machine likely stemmed from lateral movement originating from a previously compromised device.\" By that point the attacker was already running two implants on the host machine, both with system privileges. One was designed to look like Adobe software, and the other OneDrive . For the sake of persistence, the former was registered as a scheduled task set to run every five minutes.",
